# Wave T49 (Bridgeport kit): trussfloor — the IRON TRUSS DECK of Bridgeport's one bridge: dark iron deck plates crossed by two truss chords with diagonal braces and rivets. The town sign's own words made deck: 'split by its canal and joined by one iron bridge'. Worn only by the shipped span's four boardwalk cells (21,8),(22,8),(21,9),(22,9); the ferry pier keeps its wooden boardwalk — the painting's bridge is iron and its piers are wood. Registered street material for canalave beside ringfloor. No other town in the fleet walks on a truss. (NO-SAME-KIT law; WAVE-T49-BRIDGEPORT-PLAN.md §5.)
